Model crates/aura-storage/src/bridge.rs (D-E4 protections): IBC/
Tendermint-shaped light client (hash chain, ed25519 commits RFC 8032,
strictly-more-than-2/3 quorum 27/40; EVERY commit signature verified —
unknown signer / bit-flipped signature / duplicate vote = 'E9: forged
header signature (…)', no early stop), bridge protections (per-tx 1000
/ daily 1200 velocity limits, guardian pause, one-time message ids
(Nomad replay lesson), reserve invariant locked == minted (Wormhole
lesson), state-root binding), and OsClient — the AuraLite OS
finalized-checkpoint verification entry point (verify_checkpoint /
accept / check_root; 'E9: checkpoint not finalized (6)').

DoD met literally: MITM forged header -> reject (4 attack shapes in the
gate); OS client checks finalized checkpoint (forged checkpoint
rejected at the OS boundary); emulator lane green — tools/
e9_emulator_lane.py (make emulator-lane, registered in CI): E9-LANE-OK
4 (aurad --version, report --fixture, startup refusal without
--chain-id, bounded node run + clean SIGTERM). Deviation: external
AuraLite-OS / AuraLite-Emulator replaced by in-repo OsClient + aurad
lane runner.

Tests/evidence: tests/e9_bridge.rs 8 tests with metamorphic controls
(commit order, limit boundaries, determinism, quorum); 25-step scenario
digest 039d498b…39580; aggregate 4f8d9af3…575e4f; example ↔
tools/e9_bridge_check.py (RFC 8032 via cryptography) byte-identical;
tools/nc_e9.py 6/6 controls ('nc.log'); cumulative 608 NC / 31 phases.
Evidence: docs/evidence/e9/ (campaign/result.json, lane.log,
SHA256SUMS). Report: docs/ecosystem/e9-bridge-report.md. Patch:
patches/0092-E9-Bridge.patch. The bridge stays disabled on mainnet
without the H8 external audit (D-E4).
